  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Water clinics</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Vitens Evides participates in Zimbabwe on a Water Loss Reduction project financed by Zimfund or the African Development Bank Group (2016-2018). Different Vitens Experts from the Netherlands will visit Zimbabwe on specific project tasks. During these visits, the Netherlands embassy in Harare, Zimbabwe, decided to take advantage of their presence and hold four water clinics for the thirty best University water Students and eighteen officials drawn from six municipalities across the country. These trainings will be free of charge as most of the experts will be in the country on Vitens ticket.The Netherlands embassy will host four water clinics in 2018-2019. They will be held over two days for students and municipality officials in the water sector in Zimbabwe. The topics to be covered are:&#x2022;	Ground water hydrology, geo hydrology and borehole design, operations and maintenance;&#x2022;	Water quality and water treatment;&#x2022;	Finance, business planning and commercial issues: models, tariffs;&#x2022;	Non-revenue water analysis and reduction approaches: IWA water balance, District Metered Areas (DMAs);&#x2022;	Water distribution: design of networks, operations and maintenance, water meters;&#x2022;	Hydraulics: pump schemes, hydraulic models (EPAnet);&#x2022;	Geographical Information Systems (GIS);&#x2022;	Electromechanical systems: energy reduction.</narrative>
  </description>
